			(property "Description" "u-blox SAM-M10Q\n\nThe u-blox SAM-M10Q concurrent GNSS patch antenna module benefits from the exceptional performance of the u-blox M10 multi-GNSS engine. The SAM-M10Q module offers high sensitivity and minimal acquisition times in an extremely low power and ultra compact form factor.\n\nThe SAM-M10Q module utilizes concurrent reception of four GNSS systems (GPS, Galileo, GLONASS, and BeiDou), recognizes multiple constellations simultaneously and provides outstanding positioning accuracy in scenarios where urban canyon or weak signals are involved. For even better and faster positioning improvement, the SAM-M10Q features the u-blox Super-S (Super-Signal) technology, offering great RF sensitivity that can improve the dynamic position accuracy in non-line-of-sight scenarios. The SAM-M10Q also features a front-end SAW filter and an integrated LNA, ensuring excellent out-of-band jamming immunity. It also can detect jamming and spoofing attempts and report them to the host, so that the system can react to such events. The SAM-M10Q uses the latest UBX API, which is supported by https://github.com/sparkfun/SparkFun_u-blox_GNSS_v3  SparkFun's u-blox GNSS Arduino Library - v3."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
